# pnpm hoisting for Expo config plugins under the strict (default) node-linker.
#
# Some config plugins shipped by native packages — notably
# `@sentry/react-native/expo` — `require('@expo/config-plugins')` at
# prebuild/config-resolution time WITHOUT declaring it as a direct dependency
# (they treat it as provided by the Expo toolchain). Under pnpm's strict layout
# the package is only present nested under `expo`'s virtual-store entry, and
# because multiple major versions (7/8/9) coexist in the graph pnpm declines to
# auto-hoist it to `.pnpm/node_modules`. The plugin's `require` then fails with
# MODULE_NOT_FOUND both in the vitest config-plugin dry-run test and during a
# real `expo prebuild` / EAS Build.
#
# public-hoist-pattern lifts `@expo/config-plugins` into the top-level
# `node_modules`, which IS the final stop in the nested package's require
# resolution — so the plugin resolves it. pnpm hoists the version closest to the
# root (the SDK-matched one our direct devDep pins).
public-hoist-pattern[]=@expo/config-plugins
